{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung","id":356427,"title":"Unwanted Exigent Exaltations - OR - No Thanks, God of Buffalo Dung","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-01T01:12:23-08:00","id":356427,"title":"Unwanted Exigent Exaltations - OR - No Thanks, God of Buffalo Dung","content":"It's nice to be recognized, and always a welcome feeling when you realize someone sees some special potential in you, potential you might not even be aware that you possess. Becoming one of the Chosen, no matter the god, should be considered a great honor... right?<br /> <br /> Well, with the upcoming existence of Exigents, I can safely say that there are some divine empowerments I would definitely be willing to turn down.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would look first to the Discworld, specifically <b>Anoia, Goddess of Things That Get Stuck in Drawers</b>. It isn't that I don't sometimes want to get things out of drawers easier, it's just that I'm not sure I want to spend the next 3000 years traveling Creation and solving storage catastrophes with my own unique drawer-centric Charmset.<br /> <br /> What about you, kind reader? What god/goddess's offer of UNLIMITED POWER* would you probably reply to with a polite &quot;Uh, no thanks, I'm good.&quot;<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">warning-power is not actually unlimited, and may actually in many cases be very limited</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:33:55-08:00","id":356453,"title":"","content":"Personally I would worry about the price attached to being exalted by the Oh-god of Hangovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:40:54-08:00","id":356455,"title":"","content":"When Exigents drops, I'm now making Foot-In-Mouth, Exalted of Horrific Gaffe, god of &quot;that moment when you realise you should not have said that thing you just said&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As you are now, so once was I,<br /> As I am now, so you will be.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/285-andonno","name":"Andonno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:41:24-08:00","id":356456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356453#post356453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would worry about the price attached to being exalted by the Oh-god of Hangovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup,trust me. You don't want his favor<br /> <br /> And yes. I do know. Big Surprise!<br /> <br /> Says the forumite Chosen of the Lafy of Intoxicants! (I dare anybody to deny my claiam)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T01:52:13-08:00","id":356458,"title":"","content":"...I think any Exigency is a good Exigency. I mean heck, Janest is the Chosen of the God of 'those fields over there. Not all fields. Just those ones you can see over there..'.<br /> <br /> Compared to that, Anoia is a heavy-hitter, and that extra 2930 years of healthy lifespan sounds pretty sweet too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually, given Exalted can (AUIU) have metaphorical connections to their deities themes... Anoia's Chosen would unstick hearts and minds, dislodging those things that really have no place being there in the first place, and allowing us all to do what we came here to do.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the purview likely extends outwards - to solving all sorts of problems involving poor planning and lack of consideration. And even a literal reading of her domain indicates that all the *things* that get stuck in drawers are hers - so supernatural control over any knife stored poorly in a drawer. Any file filed inauspiciously.<br /> <br /> (:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:05:26-08:00","id":356463,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ultimately you're probably better off with the Exaltation of Stenchor, God of Latrines than you are as just an ordinary mortal. But, if you really don't want it, you can always kill yourself. Some people who find themselves turning into Anathema do just that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:19:30-08:00","id":356469,"title":"","content":"Presumably the gods distributing the Exigency also try to distribute their power with some care - especially the smaller, less important gods who are likely to die as a result of the process. There ought to be some loyal worshipers, or at least similarly aligned persons, to just about any purview.<br /> <br /> In terms of character design functions, likewise, you're pretty much going to get a bunch of access to excellencies is nothing else, so even if you hate the 'theme' of you exigency, that's a bunch of solid supernatural abilities (and the potential for supernatural martial arts) to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:36:42-08:00","id":356474,"title":"","content":"I feel like this is approaching Exigence and Exaltation and gods from a perspective that very few mortals would have in-setting.<br /> <br /> Spirits are wondrous and powerful and terrible and capricious and above all, not bound to human moral codes or mortal law. Most people would not think to refuse such a gift, were refusal even permitted. What horrors would their refusal of a god levy upon them, or on their loved ones? On their whole community? Maybe nothing - but that's making a bet at long odds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:41:16-08:00","id":356479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356458#post356458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I think any Exigency is a good Exigency. I mean heck, Janest is the Chosen of the God of 'those fields over there. Not all fields. Just those ones you can see over there..'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it would seem to me that when the developers say that some Exigents can be close to Solars in might, they're not always talking about those who come from the most powerful gods. The flame of the Exigency can fill the thing out a bit to bring it up to the god's needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T03:27:18-08:00","id":356523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356463#post356463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, if you really don't want it, you can always kill yourself. Some people who find themselves turning into Anathema do just that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?<br /> <br /> This would certainly make it a lot less common for Solars to kill themselves when their parents ask them if they have &quot;tried not being Anathema&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T03:33:10-08:00","id":356525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356523#post356523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. That removes a lot of potential internal narrative tension. And self-deprograming religious conceits should not be quite that easy, or quite that much like flipping a switch.<br /> <br /> Like, I don't think it's explicit when you Exalt. And I think being a Solar probably feels <i>pretty damn good </i>and different from just being a normal person, and that should give the Immaculate religious pause because you certainly probably feel (and can perform feats) above your station, comparable to the legends of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> But Solar Exaltation doesn't wipe away your personality, your cultural mores, or your pre-existing religious beliefs. If anything the fact that you still feel in control of your body and don't have irresistible urges to torture and dominate might make you <i>think</i> the religion exaggerated. But IMO it should take time for you to consider and say &quot;well, I don't feel like a demon is controlling me, I'm not just doing awful things, I have no desire to hurt people...maybe the Immaculate Order is just wrong about that stuff.&quot; But even that is a jump away from &quot;they're making it all up, the lying liars!&quot;<br /> <br /> Or you worry that the process of conversion is a slow one, you actively fight against evil thoughts and urges that your new power would make easy, when it's really your own urges and desires telling you that you have power and to exert it now.<br /> <br /> This stuff should internally work its way out gradually. And absent with being presented with hard evidence of the Sidereal creation of the Immaculates I think one would be more likely to assume that the Immaculates are misguided rather than deliberately preaching a lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T03:37:00-08:00","id":356527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356523#post356523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?<br /> <br /> This would certainly make it a lot less common for Solars to kill themselves when their parents ask them if they have &quot;tried not being Anathema&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least back in 1st edition, it was understood that some people who had just Exalted, at least in areas where the Immaculate Philosophy was powerful, would turn themselves in at the local temple to get killed, or indeed, just commit suicide before they lost themselves and turned into more of a monster.<br /> <br /> I remember Grawboski saying that one of the goals was to move Exalted away from the &quot;personal horror&quot; vibe common in many other White Wolf products, and that was one of the reasons why it was assumed that your character hadn't just Exalted a couple of days ago, but rather had been Exalted for several months at least - long enough to come to terms with his existence and not see himself as some kind of monster or regret what he had become.<br /> <br /> So when you're playing your character you're not really supposed to be having any sort of existential crisis about being a monster (unlike many other White Wolf games), but that's because your character already had it off-screen.<br /> <br /> This idea wasn't really brought up much in 2nd edition (indeed I don't know if it ever was), and I have no idea how it will work in 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> I always found it kind of interesting though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T03:55:47-08:00","id":356531,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. Thanks to both of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T06:23:42-08:00","id":356593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356523#post356523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?<br /> <br /> This would certainly make it a lot less common for Solars to kill themselves when their parents ask them if they have &quot;tried not being Anathema&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Plus there is the deferince of knowing what you were taught, and what you know in your heart. In your heart you know you are still you, and not a monster. You know that you want to do a lot of good in a world that needs it. You know this in your heart. Your mind is telling you otherwise. And these conflicts will also be interesting now to see characters come to grips with this. One of my characters Suesses Shiro a Dawn Caste Solar, was raised in a Dynastic House. Attended the House of Bells, and was raised in hopes he would exalt as a Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> He now looks back and wonders if the Immaculate scripture might be being missinterpurted. He knows his power came from the sun, and he was chosen by The UCS so he wonders, what if the first Immaculate Dragon who wrote the text had spoken metaphoricaly about the stealing of power. What if the ancient solars hadn't handled their power wisely because...they were drawn from ordinary mortals. Not people who were receiving the education needed to handle exaltation. He beleives that Solars should serve The Realm, and that the Realm needs to be rebuilt and restrengthened with clear plans for sucession. He beleives that Anathema are not demons just that the majority of them come from unprepared commoners who are not able to handle the ethical delimia that come from being exalted, because they are not raised for it. He thinks the Dragon Blooded should rule because they are born into it, and raised for it. Their children are prepared for being exalted and the ethics involved. No one can predict who will become a solar so training the common masses would be impossible. Better they learn from those raised into it.<br /> <br /> Honestly that was fun to develop in play, which is why I will enjoy 3e's you have been exlated for at most a week approach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:08:19-08:00","id":356627,"title":"","content":"Playing odd divine domains for farce never really interested me, but the idea of an unwanted Exigence does in other ways.<br /> <br /> For example, Rabszolga, God of Slavery, is an active and powerful Celestial god who turns his great power to the twin tasks of keeping slavery strong in the world and finding a way to subjugate himself into being a proper slave - and at the first one, he is wildly successful. Obviously, the Guild has a lot of work with him, so it's not hard to picture him somehow getting a black market exaltation... or, for drama points, his absolute adherence to order and submission causing him to render the Unconquered Sun some great favor (&quot;no, Lord, it was merely my place to be ripped in half by Octavian to shield those mice...&quot;) - and in either case, I'm reasonably sure that whomever he chose to bestow the Exigence upon would not be pleased, since a slave so endowed would be using the literal power of oppression, whilst anyone else would be getting power... but also a powerful mentor who believes they should strip all comforts from their lives and live as a tortured ascetic. And that's all before you even get to the logistics of using a Charm like, say, By Discipline Inured, which grants you resistance to social actions, but can only be activated by getting injured, whether by yourself or another.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I really like the idea of some warrior god of a tribe which is <i>badly</i> losing a genocidal struggle with its neighbors getting the Exigence... not for one of his own people, but for one of the enemy, both to ensure some legacy survives and because the customs she has upheld for centuries dictate that grand gifts must be given to the victor. She dies in the process of passing on this Exigence, leaving the &quot;lucky&quot; recipient, most likely the greatest hero of the victorious side, abruptly a monster tainted by strange gods and outcast from their own tribe. Awkward.<br /> <br /> That said, Chinese Mythology has left me with a powerful desire to explore the workings of gods who have &quot;un-sexy&quot; jobs, such as a divine stablemaster... who, you know, tends to Lesser Dragons. So maybe I shall have a few Exigents along those lines, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:28:09-08:00","id":356631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356593#post356593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that you want to do a lot of good in a world that needs it. </div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:46:53-08:00","id":356639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356523#post356523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?<br /> <br /> This would certainly make it a lot less common for Solars to kill themselves when their parents ask them if they have &quot;tried not being Anathema&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's sort of difficult to quantify, given that the equivalent of Solars in the classic WoD were given messages regarding the monsters around them and the Imbued themselves didn't register to the Magical Hoffman Lenses of their own kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T09:14:42-08:00","id":356646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356631#post356631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily!</div> </div> </div> </div>Good is subjective. One person might think killing off the Realm is for the good. Others might think burning down Nexus and killing the Emmassary is for the good. Good is utterly subjective in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T11:38:09-08:00","id":356723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356646#post356646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good is subjective. One person might think killing off the Realm is for the good. Others might think burning down Nexus and killing the Emmassary is for the good. Good is utterly subjective in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. Most villains don't really say &quot;I am doing this thing and it is Objectively Bad, ha ha!&quot; They think &quot;I am doing this thing, and it's unpleasant for some, but it's truly for the greater good/in my personal interest and I deserve it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T11:42:54-08:00","id":356726,"title":"","content":"Ungrateful hooligans will cower as I raise up my buffalo-dung tower to the heavens, make the fields fertile with my wretched breath, and turn back armies with filth and foul disease!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:17:14-08:00","id":356743,"title":"","content":"I would take pretty much any Exigence, but if it was something stupid and irrelevant to me I might not do a very good job protecting my patron's domain. Exalted are autonomous, so I imagine that gods will generally try to pick someone who is pretty into the subject matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:32:11-08:00","id":356778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356527#post356527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least back in 1st edition, it was understood that some people who had just Exalted, at least in areas where the Immaculate Philosophy was powerful, would turn themselves in at the local temple to get killed, or indeed, just commit suicide before they lost themselves and turned into more of a monster.<br /> <br /> I remember Grawboski saying that one of the goals was to move Exalted away from the &quot;personal horror&quot; vibe common in many other White Wolf products, and that was one of the reasons why it was assumed that your character hadn't just Exalted a couple of days ago, but rather had been Exalted for several months at least - long enough to come to terms with his existence and not see himself as some kind of monster or regret what he had become.<br /> [...]<br /> This idea wasn't really brought up much in 2nd edition (indeed I don't know if it ever was), and I have no idea how it will work in 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1<br /> <br /> The conceit that every Exalt knows inherently what they are and what that means (ergo, any Exalt who still insists they're Anathema is engaging in mentally disturbed levels of self-deception) is mostly from mid-late 2e conversations on the forums, with a little help from the bits in the 2e core that the Exaltation can see to some degree into the future of its candidate and so chooses those who *will* use that power, etc.<br /> <br /> The conversation where this all came up is also the source of Nephilpal's comment about &quot;I am so fucking metal my name is a power chord.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, the earlier assumption was that you had had the time to survive, equip yourself to some degree, and come to grips with what you were, at least to the point you wouldn't hurl yourself on the pointy end of the nearest jade daiklave with a cry of &quot;We're all over here and our secret base is highly flammable!&quot; by the end of the first session. The folks who didn't were largely not going to be PC's anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:35:18-08:00","id":356779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine that'd be a common reaction to Immaculate's that Exalt as Celestials, unless they're really really <i>really</i> deep into to the immaculate faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you mean the Immaculate <i>Philosophy</i>, not that many folks who are &quot;really really <i>really</i> deep&quot; into it would Exalt in the first place, because for mortals, one of the tenets is to basically keep your head down, stay in line, and look to the Dragon-Blooded to save the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:38:02-08:00","id":356781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Oh no, my act of Badassery has led me to become one of the dreaded Solar Anathema! ...Wait a minute, I'm still me. I don't <i>feel</i> possessed by demon sorcerer... holy Shit my religion is a lie!&quot;<br /> <br /> I imagine that'd be a common reaction to Immaculate's that Exalt as Celestials, unless they're really really <i>really</i> deep into to the immaculate faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does those kinds of narratives any kind of service when this reaction is either inherent to Exalting or condensed into moments or minutes versus being a hard struggle that some (emphasis some, not all) characters have to push through.<br /> <br /> But if you were raised a Dynast and you don't undergo this struggle, I'd say something is off. At the very least it should be in the backstory and should be something remembered. Because generally people do not cast off their lifelong religion as false without some kind of experiences and soul-searching to get them there. I don't think the intent is to treat such a thing so easily and callously. Unless of course the character only ever paid lip service and stopped being a true believer a long time ago because he didn't Exalt DB but his jerk brother did, or whatever. At any rate, that's still a moment to remember.<br /> <br /> The way you write it, it turns what might be a legitimate crisis of faith (and an interesting narrative tied to it) into a byline or worse, a joke.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine if that isn't the reaction, then for Lunars or Zeniths, what with their god attending to them after Exaltation, &quot;Your religion is a lie, Anathema are not demons and they earn the power we gave them&quot; will be pretty high up there on post exaltation infor dump.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Luna or UCS are going to give any kind of clearly-presented information in those moments. Or at least they <i>shouldn't</i>. The first interaction with the god as a Zenith or Lunar should be something mystical and ecstatic in nature, something that is remembered in a hazy and allegorical manner. Not like going to school and having a lecture that you take notes on.<br /> <br /> Your statement also rests on UCS or Luna having the particular human need to explain and comes from a very human mindset. It's important to remember that gods are not human, and even if UCS and Luna look humanoid, they're not human beings and don't approach things in the same manner that human logic would. Why would UCS care about the Immaculate Order and feel a need to info dump on you? Why would Luna bother to tell you your religious upbringing was all a falsehood? As if Exaltation is not explanation enough, or as if your future trials will not set you on the great path they hope for you and empowered you to walk.<br /> <br /> If you can, go check out <i>Houses of the Bull God</i> (1e) and note how even the highest-ranking members of the Brides of Ahlat still experience their god through ritual and hazy feelings and presences, not like they're called into his office for a &quot;state of the cult&quot; chat. That's the tone to shoot for, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T12:48:21-08:00","id":356796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356523#post356523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it a major thematic point separating <b>Exalted</b> from <b>World of Darkness</b> that as a Solar you <i>know </i>upon drawing the Second Breath that you are, in fact, not a monster even if your childhood religion has told you so?<br /> <br /> This would certainly make it a lot less common for Solars to kill themselves when their parents ask them if they have &quot;tried not being Anathema&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Some people still might kill themselves anyway because &quot;Oh god my whole life has been spent following a lie and now all of my loved ones hate me because of that lie and what is the point **** my life I'm out&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> That said, Chinese Mythology has left me with a powerful desire to explore the workings of gods who have &quot;un-sexy&quot; jobs, such as a divine stablemaster... who, you know, tends to Lesser Dragons. So maybe I shall have a few Exigents along those lines, too. </div> </div> </div>Have you tried playing Jade Empire? It is only briefly touched upon, but at one point you run into the guy in charge of keeping track of all the things you wreck and he bitches you out because you wrecked so much shit he couldn't keep up with it and was demoted for incompetence (he also mentions that one of your party members wrecks so much shit an entire department is dedicated to keeping track of it). Other celestial beings you run into have more glamorous jobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 01-01-2015, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:00:16-08:00","id":356802,"title":"","content":"Religion has managed to convince people who aren't and can't possibly be possessed, that they are in fact controlled by demons and need one or several exorcisms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure it should be different in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Not that realizing your religion is a lie should be impossible, i just don't think it's a given.<br /> <br /> As soon as you act on impulses that your faith tells you are impure or wicked, it's trivial to come to the conclusion that it's not your fault or that it's &quot;not the real you because you'd never do something like that because you are a good follower&quot;, and convince yourself that it is the influence of some demon.<br /> <br /> Edit: keeping in mind, many faiths, even (or especially) on exalted hold &quot; obedience &quot; as a virtue. Simply disobeying (because now you can) might be enough to convince oneself of demonic possession.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: and by demonic possession i also mean &quot;becoming anathema&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-01-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:05:09-08:00","id":356807,"title":"","content":"Seriously though, I picked up Jade Empire during the still ongoing Holiday sale on Steam. The game is great and I suggest that any Bioware fan who is interested in what they would do with a setting based on Eastern mysticism and kung fu pick it up. Though maybe consider buying it for the full 14.99 price from GOG if you aren't willing to tinker with things to get it running on more recent operating systems, I hear they make sure to alter their game so they are fully compatible with them. And of course once the sale ends they will be the same price so getting the GOG version will be a no brainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:30:40-08:00","id":356825,"title":"","content":"Regarding the existential crisis of Solars specifically, I think the nature of the exaltation itself has something of a self-defense mechanism built in. Solars are chosen from those with the potential and strength to become great heroes and accomplish legendary deeds. While they may be 'good' or 'evil' according to their own values they are not weak, dubious, uncertain, or self-hating. Those people become Abyssals or Infernals instead. While a Solar may be wracked with doubt as to who they are and what it means for some time, killing yourself or turning yourself in to let the Immaculate Order do it simply doesn't fit with the nature of Solar exaltation - such things should be very rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1j0RQNTrhSQVIjBJw3555qA1S9Hih1SRwychiPhEwm9k/pub\" target=\"_blank\">Whitescrub Tundra Project</a>: a fan-made setting reference for Exalted 3e.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10769032/1/\" target=\"_blank\">Edge of Underleaves</a> A pair of dragon-blooded dare the jungles of the southwest.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4060-mechalich","name":"Mechalich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4060_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"133"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:39:02-08:00","id":356831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356825#post356825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the existential crisis of Solars specifically, I think the nature of the exaltation itself has something of a self-defense mechanism built in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ex3 seems to be largely moving away from the idea of Exaltation as something designed or built with mechanisms of any sort.<br /> <br /> That said, Solar exaltation is &quot;very rare&quot; already. There's really not a big enough sample size to argue it one way or the other. And as I've pointed out prior to this, quite a lot of the Immaculate Philosophy's dogma pushes its believers <i>away</i> from personal heroism, so the number of Immaculates who Exalt as Solars in the first place to have this existential crisis is <i>vanishingly</i> small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:52:59-08:00","id":356860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356825#post356825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the existential crisis of Solars specifically, I think the nature of the exaltation itself has something of a self-defense mechanism built in. Solars are chosen from those with the potential and strength to become great heroes and accomplish legendary deeds. While they may be 'good' or 'evil' according to their own values they are not weak, dubious, uncertain, or self-hating. Those people become Abyssals or Infernals instead. While a Solar may be wracked with doubt as to who they are and what it means for some time, killing yourself or turning yourself in to let the Immaculate Order do it simply doesn't fit with the nature of Solar exaltation - such things should be very rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Flipside: Sol Chooses whom he pleases and no force in the cosmos can stay his hand when he sends the miracle of Exaltation to empower a person. You may be weak or uncertain or self-hating, but he Chose you for his own inscrutable reasons, and who are <i>you</i> to say the King of the Gods was wrong?<br /> <br /> Perhaps he anticipates you shedding your weakness, embracing your inner fire and achieving the ultimate potential he believes you possess once you truly understand what it means to be a Solar Exalt.<br /> <br /> (Statements like &quot;the Exaltation has a self-defense mechanism&quot; hit too close to 2e's &quot;magic autonomous seeker drone&quot; notion and thus stick in my craw. But I agree with your final sentence...in part because few people will really turn themselves in for punishment to a &quot;crime&quot; they do not honestly believe themselves guilty of, indoctrination or no. It's easy enough to point and say &quot;I saw Goody Osburn with the devil!&quot; but when it's you yourself that is pointed at and called Anathema, I think you approach the issue quite differently).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:12:30-08:00","id":356904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356860#post356860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps he anticipates you shedding your weakness, embracing your inner fire and achieving the ultimate potential he believes you possess once you truly understand what it means to be a Solar Exalt.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't that happen with the first Solar sorceress?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T14:18:57-08:00","id":356906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356474#post356474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip- What horrors would their refusal of a god levy upon them, or on their loved ones? On their whole community? Maybe nothing - but that's making a bet at long odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, shoot. I guess that's why all the drawers in my house were stuck when I woke up this morning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356796#post356796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip- Have you tried playing Jade Empire? -snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Jade Empire is one of my personal favorite &quot;Exalted-ish&quot; video games, really wish it had been more successful and we were swarmed with Jade Empire sequels. I choose to blame you, personally, for not buying it ten years earlier. (joking)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356726#post356726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ungrateful hooligans will cower as I raise up my buffalo-dung tower to the heavens, make the fields fertile with my wretched breath, and turn back armies with filth and foul disease!</div> </div> </div> </div>If the writers of Exigents can give the Chosen of Buffalo Dung a cool and interesting set of powers, I will be super happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:14:49-08:00","id":356959,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, my game buying abilities were limited until recently (I got a flow of income+high speed internet made it easier to find older games I didn't get when they were new and in stores).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:57:05-08:00","id":357011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=356906#post356906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the writers of Exigents can give the Chosen of Buffalo Dung a cool and interesting set of powers, I will be super happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a certain point it becomes a bit more Nobilis than Exalted, but there's never a question of <i>can</i> we do it. Just <i>should</i> we.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:32:23-08:00","id":357031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure that realizing that you are in fact still you and you are not possessed by a demon sorcerer</div> </div> </div> </div> How do you know that all of your memories up to this point weren't implanted in you five minutes ago, utterly wiping out your former persona?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:36:31-08:00","id":357034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357031#post357031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How do you know that all of your memories up to this point weren't implanted in you five minutes ago, utterly wiping out your former persona?</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of shitty incompetent demon would erase your memories and then replace them with new memories saying you had been possessed by a demon and were an abomination against the natural order that should just kill themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:00:59-08:00","id":357067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357034#post357034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of shitty incompetent demon would erase your memories and then replace them with new memories saying you had been possessed by a demon and were an abomination against the natural order that should just kill themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sort that wants you to kill yourself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:10:56-08:00","id":357075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357067#post357067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sort that wants you to kill yourself?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Order must be pretty dumb to give it exactly what it wants, then ^__^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:35:00-08:00","id":357089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357034#post357034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of shitty incompetent demon would erase your memories and then replace them with new memories saying you had been possessed by a demon and were an abomination against the natural order that should just kill themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If I was controlling your mind, would you doubt me?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:36:54-08:00","id":357091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357089#post357089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;If I was controlling your mind, would you doubt me?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=62gzsqwEZCM\" data-code=\"62gzsqwEZCM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/62gzsqwEZCM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T22:13:23-08:00","id":357235,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that being the exalt of a narcotics deity may not be particularly appealing to some people. On the other hand it would justify playing as Snowflame and I don't think I can argue against that kind of insane glory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T22:29:59-08:00","id":357238,"title":"","content":"Are we really so certain that the god who provides the exigence limits it in as objectionable a way as all these jokes seem to suggest?<br /> <br /> The exalted of the god of buffalo dung will probably have almost no ability to directly affect buffalo dung, this isn't bending after all. Powers would probably be over waste and decay, perhaps &quot;growing&quot; into renewal and power from humble places (fertilizer, burning it for cheap heat for the poor, dung beetles, etc.)<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Incarnae might crack some jokes about the source of the power, but they will still respect the power to ruin enemies and the recover from bad circumstances. Those running from the Wyld Hunt might be positively grateful for &quot;No Glance Spared for Filth&quot; that lets them slip away unseen because they are so far beneath notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T22:44:28-08:00","id":357264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I may or may not have been exaggerating how quickly one would make the realization, but I figure that realizing that you are in fact still you and you are not possessed by a demon sorcerer should be the sort of thing that shakes your faith enough to question if your religion is truthful and walk away from it(well, if they were wrong about something <i>this </i>important...)</div> </div> </div> </div>People with an incredibly strong expectation that something will happen can certainly have their beliefs shaken. However, they are quite a bit more likely than you're suggesting to try rationalizing away the disconnect, to find some way it was true in broad strokes, even if the particulars are off. &quot;Perhaps one doesn't fall prey immediately. Why would the teachings not reveal this...? Hm, of course; even if not immediate, it is surely inevitable. Better that they view me as a monster with my face now, to stop me before the demon takes full hold.&quot; That strikes me as a pretty legitimate thought a character might have early on.<br /> <br /> I mean, the Immaculates have every incentive to spread horror stories of the Anathema, including those of staggering and subtle persuasive abilities that lead even righteous mortal men to turn their backs on all they believed without ever realizing the cause. In the face of such, the idea that the demon's possession could take a form just as subtle isn't far-fetched. There's also the matter of past-life memory flashes. Whether an Exalt perceives them as things that happened to him personally or to someone else, one who had believed in Immaculate teachings can pretty easily turn them in favor of dreading a demon's possession. &quot;The demon must be stirring, at last. It shows me stories... A life I feel-- I <i>know</i> was mine. The demon is canny; I know these are lies -- they must be! -- but they feel so... <i>true</i>. I can't have much time. Dragons, when I am under its thrall, will I even notice?&quot;<br /> <br /> That I tend to imagine the use of Exalted power to feel very natural, perhaps even pleasant, while the possession of the Anathema's power has been long taught to be starkly against the natural order could well lend credence to the &quot;demon be crazy subtle&quot; conclusion's plausibility in the mind of such an adherent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I figure &quot;My deads have led Luna/The Unconquered Sun to empower me and lift me to divine status&quot; to be something to take away from being attended to by those Deities, which of course precludes &quot;I've been body jacked by a demon sorcerer that stole power from the Moon/Sun&quot;. </div> </div> </div>See &quot;really likely to try rationalizing away the unexpected&quot; above. Such Exalted behold a transcendantally glorious entity visiting them, likely far beyond anything else ever witnessed outside their dreams. That it was a magnificent deception brought on by the possessing demon known to be of vast power isn't an unreasonable conclusion for an Immaculate faithful.<br /> <br /> It really doesn't strike me as at all surprising that these are thoughts some of the newly Chosen might have. For some Exalted, these thoughts may get them killed, though likelier less from suicide or turning themselves over than from distraction -- struggling with intense self-doubt can easily lead one to make mistakes. These thoughts aren't going to be common among most longer-lived Exalted (such as PCs who've been Chosen for at least a year) in part from natural selection. Of those who originally thought that way, Exalts who ultimately came to view things differently have one less factor working against them, and those who lacked such views in the early going aren't terribly likely to take them up later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T01:50:34-08:00","id":357345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you manifest powers before the demon took control? Why would the deception take the form of Luna or Ignis Divine instead of one of the Immaculate Dragons(who of course, the immaculate faithful would place higher than the other two)?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Immaculate Order the Anathema were powerful Yozi servants who stole the powers of the Sun and the Moon (the leaders of Heaven - the Immaculate Dragons are the lords of Terrestrial world - the Dragons aren't subservient to Yu-Shan, rather the gods of Yu-Shan labor to ensure the safety and prosperity of Creation) and made it their own.<br /> <br /> When you become Anathema, the soul of those ancient beings, along with the stolen power, fuses with you and will slowly take control. You won't notice anything at first - indeed, often times the Anathema are shining champions and paragons of heroism. They are, often wonderful people, initially. But over time they become corrupted by those ancient souls, as well as become more and more powerful. Eventually the Anathema's soul takes full control, and they turn into monsters and tyrants, who will destroy all their care about, and there is nothing that can be done to stop this. Try as they might to fight this, that is the ultimate fate of the Anathema.<br /> <br /> As such, the Anathema need to be killed quickly, before they grow more powerful, even if they do present themselves as heroes right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Those who believe in the Immaculate Philosophy could easily take any flashes of insight or words of their divine patron to be tricks and deception caused by the soul of the ancient Anathema who is trying to subsume control of their body and spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T02:22:47-08:00","id":357352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of shitty incompetent demon would erase your memories and then replace them with new memories saying you had been possessed by a demon and were an abomination against the natural order that should just kill themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div> I was not saying that that was something that an Immaculate might assert had happened to you, it was a thought exercise to illustrate the fragility and uncertainty of thought and memory, something frequently illustrated in various forms of mental illness. My point is that the logic of &quot;huh, I don't <i>feel</i> like I've been possessed, so obviously Immaculate dogma is phoney&quot; is fallacious, because hey, what kind of shitty demon makes it really obvious that you've been possessed, such that you have no compunctions about killing yourself? To people who've read Fullmetal Alchemist, think of it like Wrath, who has memories of his prior life but can't really tell if his current personality comes from that soul or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T07:45:40-08:00","id":357462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may or may not have been exaggerating how quickly one would make the realization, but I figure that realizing that you are in fact still you and you are not possessed by a demon sorcerer should be the sort of thing that shakes your faith enough to question if your religion is truthful and walk away from it(well, if they were wrong about something <i>this </i>important...)</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you know you're not possessed by a demon sorcerer?<br /> <br /> No, really. Is it supposed to announce itself? Or is it possibly insidious enough to slowly co-opt you without you knowing it? Why would it say &quot;hey I'm here?&quot; Is not the presence of strange power enough to convince you that you are not really the same person you were ten minutes ago?<br /> <br /> I'm sure the Immacualtes preach that Anathema try to lie and say that there's nothing wrong with them, they're still themselves. &quot;These are lies to test your faith and make you lower your guard. Do not believed their honeyed lies!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I figure &quot;My deads have led Luna/The Unconquered Sun to empower me and lift me to divine status&quot; to be something to take away from being attended to by those Deities, which of course precludes &quot;I've been body jacked by a demon sorcerer that stole power from the Moon/Sun&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your first sentence is a setting premise OOC. Most people don't know this IC. You are looking at Exaltation through a far too logical/rational lens. It is a miraculous religious experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you manifest powers before the demon took control?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you <i>know</i> it's not in control? You can assume, but you can't <i>know</i>.<br /> <br /> But now you have these super powers and can do things you couldn't before...so you do them. You exert your power to get what you want; even if it's to help people, can you see how others might view it as being controlled, stepping outside the proscribed social order, wielding a fire that was never meant for human hands?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the deception take the form of Luna or Ignis Divine instead of one of the Immaculate Dragons(who of course, the immaculate faithful would place higher than the other two)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people don't know about Luna or UCS directly. It's been stated for 3e that there is not really much worship of UCS <i>anywhere </i>since the Usurpation or at least the Contagion; it's done to the Dragons.<br /> <br /> See also: Perfect Soul finds an old unused altar of UCS in her occupied homeland that she smashes in frustration and thereby Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And really, to be attended to by a Deity seems like it'd be more than just a few flashes of vaugly remembered something something, especially for an Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What is gained by getting a lecture infodump compared to a true religious experience? I say <i>absolutely nothing</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to The Ask the Devs thread on RPGnet, Exalts can't become Gods because Becoming a God and Becoming an Exalt are both forms of Divine Uplifting, and to be divinely uplifted is to be made a divine entity, meaning that an Exalt is a Divinity and thus while they are not the equal of Sol or Luna, they are, at least, a peer, and a peer sorta deserves an actual conversation, don't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is tortured logic. What's with the notion that Exalted deserve to be treated in any particular way by the patrons? You don't deserve anything. You just received the greatest miracle in the world and you want an instruction manual, ownership guide, and truth primer? God, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Luna might be fickle, but I figure Sol would explain a few things to the Zennith's he's attending to, if only because the Zennith will probably be scared and/or confused and The Unconcord Sun, even if compassion is not a virtue mechanically, as a God who embodies Virtue is probably very compassionate(hell, that's why the New Token Zennith was Exalted in the first place)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would he explain anything? The gift of his Exaltation is explanation enough.<br /> <br /> You simply <i>cannot</i> approach the motivations and expressions of these gods like you would other humans. To do so immeasurably lessons the notion of &quot;religious experience&quot; and the notion of the scope of these gods. Being attended to by Ahlat for the Brides or UCS/Luna for their respective Exalts should be an experience like Moses and the Burning Bush, like Muhammad at Mount Hira, like Joan of Arc. These are emotionally evocative images. Some 4-armed gold guy walking up and telling you, in no uncertain terms, what the world is &quot;really&quot; about and that your old faith is a lie...that's not evocative at all. That's narrative- and exposition-killing deus ex machina.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of feal's like a waste of an Exaltation though, for it to go towards someone who'll off themselves when they realize what they are.<br /> <br /> I'd figure fate or something would keep people from exalting if they were just going to waste the power of the Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it a waste? If the person does that, Sol will empower someone else. Not even he can predict how you'll respond to power 100%. Whether you commit suicide or get offed by local monks who witness your ascension, no real skin off his nose.<br /> <br /> And Exaltation explicitly breaks the chains of destiny imposed on mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-02-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T11:18:40-08:00","id":357634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357238#post357238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we really so certain that the god who provides the exigence limits it in as objectionable a way as all these jokes seem to suggest?<br /> <br /> The exalted of the god of buffalo dung will probably have almost no ability to directly affect buffalo dung, this isn't bending after all. Powers would probably be over waste and decay, perhaps &quot;growing&quot; into renewal and power from humble places (fertilizer, burning it for cheap heat for the poor, dung beetles, etc.)<br /> <br /> The chosen of the Incarnae might crack some jokes about the source of the power, but they will still respect the power to ruin enemies and the recover from bad circumstances. Those running from the Wyld Hunt might be positively grateful for &quot;No Glance Spared for Filth&quot; that lets them slip away unseen because they are so far beneath notice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure the Exigent of Buffalo Dung has all kinds of amazing powers, but the anima banner <i>sucks</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T12:12:17-08:00","id":357647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357634#post357634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sure the Exigent of Buffalo Dung has all kinds of amazing powers, but the anima banner <i>sucks</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but how much intimidation could you wring out of the threat that if your opponent loses they lost to a guy empowered by a literal crap deity. There's bound to be a few people in the terrestrials that would have to think about that fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T12:42:36-08:00","id":357659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sort of getting the mental imagie of a hypothetical Elder Essence Exigent of cow Dung gaining the ability to see through lies because they're a load of bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I get the feeling that would be a standard power in their investigation tree.<br /> The theme being &quot;dealing with bull shit&quot;. (Likewise, in larceny, they'd be able to improvise the best bullshit. Presence would allow them to cut the crap, Socialize would let them clean up a shitty society, etc.<br /> <br /> Although that depends if they have Ability Charms, or Literally-Covered-In-Different-Kinds-of-Shit charms, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":".  typos 01-02-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T12:46:09-08:00","id":357660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elder essence has gone from &quot;The same but stronger&quot; to &quot;Charms that diverge from theme, slightly&quot;, right? I fingure a suficiently powerful Elder Exigent probably qualifies as having &quot;<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SemanticSuperpower\" target=\"_blank\">Semantic Super Powers</a>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I *think* elder Essence has gone from &quot;a fuckton of power creeping tricks that defines an entirely new level of play and then says it's the One True Way to Play&quot; to &quot;stuff that makes your fundamental E1-5 Charm competencies easier/cheaper to use and/or able to use more often.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T13:09:22-08:00","id":357677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that I still have my own memories and motivations?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really proof as nobody can verify it but you. That's testimony, and could be a an honest misinterpretation or an intentional lie. Nobody has said that all &quot;Anathema possession&quot; feels the same. In fact, it's smart to mention all kinds of ways it might feel, to cover as many bases as possible, so that people give confession or tell on friends who are behaving strangely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And &quot;Miraculous religious experience&quot; precludes it being demonic possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is going to take your word for it IC when you say you had a miraculous religious experience that sounds, to people indoctrinated by the Immaculates, as Anathema possession. The Immaculates have had the better part of two millennia to speak agains the Solars and Lunars. I think it's silly to think they haven't come up with explanations to common questions. <br /> <br /> OOC it doesn't matter because OOC we know it's not demonic possession.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Sol personally tends to his Zenith's, and in the first age atleast they were meant to be his High Priests. Why else would he attend to them if not to explain what the fuck just happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he wants to. Why does he need a reason? Giving them huge amounts of exposition, versus visions the ST can later reference or some kind of inspiration or whatever is boring and quite ill-fitting the mythic inspirations for Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just impressed one of the Gods enough to be made a divinity in your own right. You probably don't realize what's happened untill after the fact, and if you were an immaculate, it probably happened against your will. As a divinity, you are, while by no means his equal, one of that Deity's peers. Luna might be fickle enough to not care, but God of Virtue and Light Sol will probably at least assuage the fears of the Zenith he's attending to, if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>A baby Solar is in no way UCS's peer. For that matter, a 1000-year-old Solar is in no way UCS's peer, even if he thinks he is and even if mortals perceive him to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in 2E at least, the Solars had the right to Enter Yu Shan. If you have the right to enter the home of the gods, you have the right to a conversation instead of a fever dream</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not good logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, or at least the spark notes. This is a power that lets me rival that of some of the strongest gods if applied right. If I'm being attended to by the god who game me mine, I'm asking for an explanation so I don't accidentally kill somebody while trying to figure out how my super kung fu works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't understand why. This isn't how mystery religions, cults, or any person ever describing a religious experience has, well, described it. There's no good reason at all to deviate from that broad base of IRL influence. Story-wise, there's nothing to gain and a lot of potential to lose. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'm the king of the gods. There are hundreds of bits of my power that go out and empower mortals, turning them into divinities themselves. I personally attend to one fifth of them, and that fifth in ages past served as my high priests. I don't tell them jack shit about their new literally godlike powers, because I like to see them struggle&quot; Sounds a bit dickish for the guy who was born so that the king of dickbags had someone to oppose. Also, I remember reading that during the Primordial War, Sol gave himself over as a prisoner to the Primordials in exchange for the life of a single non exalted human. If true, then for him to do that and then not explain anything to the Zenith who is freaking the fuck out because his religion preaches that he's a monster sounds majorly OOC.</div> </div> </div> </div>First you're coming across like Charms are something Exalted do like push a button, as opposed to being natural outgrowths of their existing skills. If you already know how to pull a bow or preach to a crowd, your Charms are not internally going to feel like you're switching them on. It's like drawing a breath and doing it normally, except now it's simply better. That doesn't require an instruction manual. And again it certainly does not benefit the mythic tone of the game if the heroes get the whole world and objective truth laid out to them as part of a backstory. Not every character is going to struggle, but some logically would, and it does not do justice to those narratives to render them into stupid footnotes rather than transformative experiences. What is more meaningful to you: possibly gradually figuring out your childhood religion was based on untruths and crusading forward to purse those who lie to millions, or getting a Spark Notes to Being UCS's Priest and having it all explained to you in 3 minutes? The latter is frankly just kind of chumpy. There's no story there. There's no discovery. Just a shitty cutscene. <br /> <br /> Also seriously that single mortal story was and is totally nonsensical and stupid. &quot;Oh millions of people are dying but I can't fight directly (but can do any number of other things, though I won't) so I'll hostage myself for this one guy?&quot; Come on. I mean, I get what the point was: how epic Compassion and Conviction can override epic common sense. But it did nothing for me. I'm not saying you're a bad or stupid person if it did something for you though, just that it did nothing for me and looked like some wankery. Out of all the things UCS COULD do that wouldn't violate his oath, that's what he does? That, instead of finding a way to protect people caught in the path of the War? It comes across as totally self-indulgent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and God as the Burning Bush actually told moses stuff. God, supposedly told Joan of Arc to lead the French. I don't know enough about Islam to talk about Muhammad, but I'm pretty sure Allah's messengers told him stuff too.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're talking rather general (but personally poignant) messages versus &quot;hey your religion is a lie, also blah blah blah world exposition info.&quot; Moses didn't need to be told his god was the One True God; he already knew that - what he received was God's gift of Law. Joan didn't need to be told that God was on her side, but her experience inspired her to buck social custom and become a female warrior and leader. Muhammad was already a pious person before Gabriel spoke to him. <br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that we're talking about different things and different interactions. I really don't like the idea that UCS is going to appear to a Zenith and read the objective, OOC History and Setting chapter of Exalted 3e to the Zenith to &quot;get him up to speed.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Brides of Ahlat are mortals. a half remembered fever dream is probably all they can take. The Zenith Caste of The Solar Exalted, the Chosen of the Unconquered Sun, are not mortals, not any more. They are a full fledged Divinity now, albeit of a different sort than the gods. &quot;I'm the king of the gods. Your deeds have impressed me, so I've granted you power and the potential for more and the ability to gain great wisdom. PS. You are now a deity, albeit of a different sort than most, with the rights that entails and the responsibility to do good, as you see it, with your new abilities&quot; while probably not said in those words, is something you should be able to take away from being attended to after being turned into a god in mortal flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah we're just gonna have to disagree. It doesn't matter to me if we're talking Ahlat/mortal bride or UCS/Zenith. We're not talking about having tea in an office with a god as a Sidereal would. We're talking an epic vision of inspiration. Solars can go to Yu-Shan and I'd be hella disappointed if the default response was a jaded one, rather than one of wonder and terror, even as an Exalt, until they got used to it through repeated trips. <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Rater202;n357619]For one, it presumably takes time for Lytek to scrub an exaltation clean or do whatever it is he needs to do to get them ready for another host, so if he gets it back immediately, that's wasted effort on his part and probably a lot of paper work since Heaven's a Bureaucracy.&quot;Send that one out, okay what's next? File some paperwork to get that bitch off my ass, approve vacation time for one of my underlings... check the cabinet for...What the Fuck I just sent that one out!&quot; It'd only happen one or two times before Lytek sent a meme up to the big guy.[/quote<br /> Fuck Lytek.<br /> <br /> Seriously fuck Lytek and all the dumbass shit attributed to him for 2 editions. He's a jumped-up bureaucrat who should have precisely zero influence on Exaltations. Fuck his cabinet while we're at it, there are a million more evocative ways to describe what happened to the Solars and they all involve UCS and not Siderelas jumping some Vegeta-lookalike to get in his filing cabinet. Also you think UCS gives to fucks how much paperwork Lytek has to do? No.<br /> <br /> I hope Lytek's role vis a vis Exaltations is completely excised what with Exaltations going back to being personally bestowed rather than 2e's autonomous drones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but looking at the fate of a mortal could tell you what sort of person he was, is, and would have been absent the exaltation, and that could give a you a good idea of whether or not he's open minded enough to accept that he hasn't been body jacked by a demon sorcerer when confronted with evidence that his religion may have been wrong about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate also isn't UCS's bag, for what it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T14:20:58-08:00","id":357735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will, and that's enough. You personally, the guy who just had an intense religious experience and was then personally attended to by one of the mightiest of the Celestial Gods, will know that you're not a demon that jacked some guys body. That's what's important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you though? How do you differentiate the experiences? You only have your subjective feelings to go on, and there's a tenet that says you might feel that way.<br /> <br /> Identity and how Exaltation changes it have always been important themes of Exalted and I don't think it does the game or potential narratives any justice to hand players a straight answer on a silver platter like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;BY the way, you're not possessed by a demon, you're still you&quot; is not huge amounts of exposition, and something I'd take for a certainty that the High Priest of the Unconquered Sun could take away from being attended to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'd think it weird if the UCS was completely up to date on specific religious tenets of Creation's religions. He turned his back. He vaguely knows bad things are happening, but even in perfect compassion he set himself away from the world and can't bring himself to turn back for a long time. But somehow he knows or cares about the details of one fucked-up religion? Again this is applying a lot of human logic to an issue that is about faith, not reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Divinity is not the peer of a divinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is super duper false equivalency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd think that using your essence to shoot better to be something you do consciously, even if you don't strictly need to be taught how to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how it's really mentioned as working though. It's fundamental to the shift from &quot;native Charms as Techniques&quot; (which was somewhat explicit in 2e) versus &quot;native Charms as outgrowths of pre-existing personal puissance.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also strongly dislike the idea of a supposedly perfect being like Sol acting like an Idiot, and if you're personally attending to one of Your High Priests right after you'e transformed them into a divinity, and they come from a culture that believes that being with their powers are monsters to be destroyed, then the smart thing to do is tell the guy &quot;Your not a monster, your one of my exalted. Like the Dragonblooded, but different.&quot; and not just dick around and let him go off himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno why Sol would be super involved in knowing where this guy came from either to be honest. There's a moment of brilliance that attracts attention. It's a miracle. But I don't think Sol reads the guy's history somehow. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It is I, Sol Invictus the Unconquered Sun, King of the Gods. Your act of [X] has impressed me to the point where I have made you a divine being and my champion&quot; Is pretty general, but personally poignant, information, and a meeting with Sol should not be the kind of thing you can rationalize away as a demonic deception.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is way too much of a human interaction for me. I feel like UCS's presence should be intense and awe-inspiring and even difficult to be in, even for his Chosen. Because they're still men, where he never was. <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think of a book or game or something I saw, where a character would experience some supernatural thing and in the aftermath, the human mind would invent a story to make sense of it, being unable to process the actual raw data perceived by the senses. I think this might be what it's like to be in the presence of UCS: allegory is necessary to make sense of perfection, such being a thing the human mind has a hard time envisioning. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to be seriously misunderstanding my point. If A Zenith being attended to by Sol, or if a Lunar being attended to by Luna, is a deep religious experience that occurs shortly after you yourself become, for all intents and purposes, a god in mortal form, then by all means it should be the sort of thing that makes sure that you <b>Know </b>that you have become a divine being and are now their champion, not something you can rationalize away, and a half remembered fever dream is something you can rationalize away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't think so and I've never read anything leading me to believe this is how it works.<br /> <br /> The closest thing we get, IIRC, is with Panther, and again IIRC it's nothing like you described. Nothing is really explained to him (and I mean the circumstances are also questionably heroic but) that is a whole other thing). Please correct me if I'm wrong, my memories on this are hazy and I'm away from books. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally all Lytek does is scrub down the exaltations down so that bits of memory and personality from the last guy doens't screw up the next guy. He has control over who gets the exaltation.<br /> <br /> The fact that Past Life Memories in the Solars is a thing that happens tells me that scraping away the personality of the last guy is probably something that needs to be done, especially because First Age Solars were dicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a solid &quot;meh&quot; from me on this. One could get rid of &quot;memory fragments stick to the Exaltation&quot; pretty easily if one was so inclined and that would be that. Or passing back through Sol's hands erases everything but some very ingrained memories which appear in dreams. That's more elegant than creepy uncle Vegeta bonsai man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something has to keep the Solars Exalting while Sol isn't paying attention. If Sol's will functions to exalt mortals even when he is not consciously paying attention to Creation, then it's not meaningfully different than a semi autonomous system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is <i>extremely</i> thematically different though. I think the writers would agree, otherwise there wouldn't be a change from the 2e portrayal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cosmic X-Box has limited controllers. It's not hard to believe that at some point Sol and one of the Maiden's both had a turn away, and Sol was like &quot;Hey, *Maiden*? Would you mind, when you get the chance, tinkering with the loom a bit so that people who'll kill themselves after realizing they've become one of my champions won't be in a position to do deeds to Earn my Exaltation? I don't like attending to my Zenith's only for them to wave me off as a demonic deception and kill themselves when I leave because they were raised by those silly immaculate&quot;<br /> &quot;Should I do the same for Luna's Chosen as well?&quot;<br /> &quot;Sure, why not!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, do what you want with your head/table canon but that stuff is not remotely evidence to support your position.<br /> <br /> Also makes UCS way too knowledgeable about Creation events after turning his face.<br /> <br /> Also removes the chance for stories where Exalts may struggle with their identity, do great deeds, but ultimately be full of despair and try end it somehow (and that process may be exactly what they need to finally &quot;wake up&quot;).<br /> <br /> Way more is lost than is gained.<br /> <br /> And again Exaltation largely breaks the destiny on mortals, it's why (in the past at least) Essence-users can screw up whole cities worth of destiny, because the &quot;plan&quot; for the mortal lives (or whatever, fucking not-predestination-but-also-kinda-predestination inconsistent writing can go to hell) pretty much become unpredictable after Exaltation due to being a thing that can both wield Essence (like gods) but has no inherent purpose fundamental to its existence (unlike gods).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T15:56:50-08:00","id":357836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Five Elemental Dragons who are either Gaia's Children or Her Devas depending on edition are the so called Immaculate Dragons, yes? And they take Gaia's Turns at the games for her, yes? </div> </div> </div>0 for 2, there, sport.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T16:26:05-08:00","id":357885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a suicidally depressed Solar does not sound like the kinda person who'd be fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone wants to play a suicidally depressed Solar.<br /> <br /> In the first Exalted game I ran the Eclipse Caste and the Fire Aspect had been childhood sweethearts until she Exalted as a Fire Aspect and ended up adopted into House Tepet. 10 years later he's on the Isle trying to argue some bullshit dock tax with a corrupt official and ends up Exalting as a Solar, he's bombarded with memories that aren't his own and decides that the thing he wants more than anything in the world is to find her and let her judge be the judge of if he's still himself or not.<br /> <br /> The fact he was prepared to die if she deemed it necessary later became an experience he drew upon when dealing with the Moonshadow who was rather crazy in a hated herself and was prone to self harming kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T16:33:21-08:00","id":357886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung#post356427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice to be recognized, and always a welcome feeling when you realize someone sees some special potential in you, potential you might not even be aware that you possess. Becoming one of the Chosen, no matter the god, should be considered a great honor... right?<br /> <br /> Well, with the upcoming existence of Exigents, I can safely say that there are some divine empowerments I would definitely be willing to turn down.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would look first to the Discworld, specifically <b>Anoia, Goddess of Things That Get Stuck in Drawers</b>. It isn't that I don't sometimes want to get things out of drawers easier, it's just that I'm not sure I want to spend the next 3000 years traveling Creation and solving storage catastrophes with my own unique drawer-centric Charmset.<br /> <br /> What about you, kind reader? What god/goddess's offer of UNLIMITED POWER* would you probably reply to with a polite &amp;quot;Uh, no thanks, I'm good.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">warning-power is not actually unlimited, and may actually in many cases be very limited</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no to Blek, Goddess of Used Tampons, Jorsh, God of Too Much Information, Halb, God of Wondering Where That Stench Is Coming From, and Shob, God of Unpaid Interns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T16:41:36-08:00","id":357892,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a suicidally depressed Solar does not sound like the kinda person who'd be fun to play. You want drama from an immaculate Exalting as a Solar &quot;Wait, if my faith was wrong about this, then what else could they have been wrong about?&quot; and then struggling with that. Ooh, or maybe they're favorite Uncle or their twin brother exalted as a Dragon Blooded and is leading a wyld hunt against them. That's something to angst about that isn't anywhere near as stupid as &quot;wow is me, I've been replaced with a body jacking demon, even though I have all the same memories and motivations as I did before, don't feel like doing any of the suff the immaculate order said we do, and don't remember being a demon sorcerer or jacking anybodies&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok first you are oversimplifying the outcome of a solar not instantly knowing the whole immaculate faith is a lie thing. First they can exalt and not know it happened.I believe in one of the novels Demeth spent some time after he exalted convinced he had suffered heat stroke and that accounted for the vision. Hell the thing you said where the vision includes Sol doing an info dump, on how the main religion is a lie and he's the king of the gods who has chosen you to do great deeds, would probably make people more suspicious as its kind of a lot of random specific denial. More likely you'd at least get the desired response out of &quot;people are in trouble you have power now move!&quot;<br /> <br /> There's also character potential in just thinking the demon hasn't overwhelmed you and wanting to do what good you can before you fall to the taint. As for why you would have power before you were overtaken, well when you are still yourself mostly human actions will be taken that can be studied and used for later interactions after you've fallen. That's assuming the exalt doesn't think they'll end up with something like a coadjutor whispering in their ear. I mean it wouldn't be too hard to imagine there's a fair number of stories regarding demons and rhaksha I don't think it would be too unreasonable for a person to think its studying your actions to prevent future detection. Not to mention you not being a horrific monster might damage the immaculate faith which will be more helpful to it in the future.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just, from my hyper logical perspective, sounds like the only way you could angst about it would be if you were very thoroughly brainwashed by the sham religion of the realm(in which case, ou wouldn't have exalted because the actions that make you eligible for exaltation involve moving beyond your station) or if you're holding a massive idiot ball.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually while the immaculate faith does preach that one should avoid going above their station it doesn't specifically forbid striving for excellence or the like, so it doesn't forbid anything that would potential lead to exaltation. (Outside of trying to oppose or overthrow the DBs of course.) Heck at least one story had a terrestrial chastising a soldier for fleeing from a failed wyld hunt saying something to the effect of, &quot;Its a known fact that those who do well and die fighting the anathema will be rewarded by being reborn as one of the dragonblood in the next life.&quot; So yeah that argument doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T18:05:13-08:00","id":357926,"title":"","content":"So, I just had a thought on what might be an interesting concept. A a follower of the immaculate faith who exalts and, instead of coming to the realization that solars/lunars aren't demons, decides that that they are either some sort of special case resisting possession or that <i>they</i> have been blessed by the sun/moon....But for the purpose of hunting down all of those jerks who <i>stole</i> the power from them. Perhaps they exalted while fighting off some asshole Solar/Lunar attacking their village and use this as evidence that they are chosen but others are demons with stolen power, as an example of possible backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T18:21:43-08:00","id":357932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357885#post357885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone wants to play a suicidally depressed Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I dunno. Wish fulfillment sorta thing, maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T18:40:42-08:00","id":357938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357932#post357932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I dunno. Wish fulfillment sorta thing, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've done it in gunstar authotonia, but then again I was playing the equivalent of Riggs from lethal weapon 1.<br /> <br /> He'd just lost his wife and his sense of sight on the frount lines fighting the unconquered sun. <br /> <br /> It was a very rewarding character, but it was hard sometimes.<br /> <br /> Plus your kinda meant to be losing in gunstar, your running away. Desperatly searching for a way to turn around and bring the fight back to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2129-steel_in_sea","name":"Steel_in_sea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:13:54-08:00","id":357986,"title":"","content":"So, while this is still thoroughly in the realm of this thread's derail, I took a 4-5 hour drive today and worked through some podcasts. Among these was the TED Radio Hour, including an interesting <a href=\"http://www.ted.com/talks/lesley_hazleton_the_doubt_essential_to_faith\" target=\"_blank\">one by Lesley Hazleton</a>, who authored a biography of Muhammad. One section in particular struck me as relevant to this derail:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lesley Hazleton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[A] human encountering the divine, as Muslims believe Muhammad did, to the rationalist, this is a matter not of fact but of wishful fiction, and like all of us, I like to think of myself as rational.<br /> <br /> Which might be why when I looked at the earliest accounts we have of that night, what struck me even more than what happened was what did not happen. Muhammad did not come floating off the mountain as though walking on air. He did not run down shouting, &quot;Hallelujah!&quot; and &quot;Bless the Lord!&quot; He did not radiate light and joy. There were no choirs of angels, no music of the spheres, no elation, no ecstasy, no golden aura surrounding him, no sense of an absolute, fore-ordained role as the messenger of God. That is, he did none of the things that might make it easy to cry foul, to put down the whole story as a pious fable. Quite the contrary. In his own reported words, he was convinced at first that what had happened couldn't have been real. At best, he thought, it had to have been a hallucination -- a trick of the eye or the ear, perhaps, or his own mind working against him. At worst, possession -- that he'd been seized by an evil jinn, a spirit out to deceive him, even to crush the life out of him. In fact, he was so sure that he could only be majnun, possessed by a jinn, that when he found himself still alive, his first impulse was to finish the job himself, to leap off the highest cliff and escape the terror of what he'd experienced by putting an end to all experience.<br /> <br /> So the man who fled down the mountain that night trembled not with joy but with a stark, primordial fear. He was overwhelmed not with conviction, but by doubt. And that panicked disorientation, that sundering of everything familiar, that daunting awareness of something beyond human comprehension, can only be called a terrible awe.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Yet whether you're a rationalist or a mystic, whether you think the words Muhammad heard that night came from inside himself or from outside, what's clear is that he did experience them, and that he did so with a force that would shatter his sense of himself and his world and transform this otherwise modest man into a radical advocate for social and economic justice. Fear was the only sane response, the only human response.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if I'd completely agree that fear was the <i>only</i> response, but it and doubt are categorically legitimate ones. And if one just doesn't think that the tale of Muhammad receiving the revelation is good inspiration for a Zenith Exaltation, then... Well, I don't know what to say to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Small adjustment. 01-02-2015, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:25:59-08:00","id":357992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe the concerns about being possessed there came <i>without</i> adhering to a religion that spells out possession as a thing that happens. </div> </div> </div>Actually, belief in possession by Djinn was quite common at the time, in Arabia. There were a lot of mystics and poets who claimed to be possessed by djinn, and that's what he suspected might have happened to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T20:57:59-08:00","id":358000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357992#post357992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, belief in possession by Djinn was quite common at the time, in Arabia. There were a lot of mystics and poets who claimed to be possessed by djinn, and that's what he suspected might have happened to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I freely admit my ignorance of whatever beliefs Muhammad followed in his early years. As well as much else about the man's life, for that matter. &gt;.&gt; I'll retract that statement; the parallelism I was going for between djinn possession and Immaculate claims of demon possession are obvious enough not to need pointing out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T01:06:54-08:00","id":358120,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think it's still a pretty valid point, perhaps more valid. His worry that he might have been possessed by a Djinn and not really chosen by Allah to become the Seal of the Prophets, is probably the best parallel you're likely to get between Solar Exaltation and a real person's experiences.<br /> <br /> As to the beliefs he'd previously practiced, Muhammed and his tribe were all pagans (the Kabbah, the big black rock in Mecca, was a centre of pagan worship), but the southern Arabs had for a while been Jews, and there were a number of northern tribes who were Christians. While Muhammed's family weren't Judeo-Christian, he'd almost certainly have met many Jews and Christians in his life, so figures such as the Angel Gabriel were presumably familiar to him before he started preaching monotheism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-03-2015, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T02:09:35-08:00","id":358157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a suicidally depressed Solar does not sound like the kinda person who'd be fun to play.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't get it when people say stuff like this. It would seem to me that the point of roleplaying is that it's a safe way to approximate the whole amazing, diverse range of contexts and experiences. Suicidally depressed people exist, and have experiences worth considering, so why <i>not</i> try to get in their mindsets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T02:39:15-08:00","id":358167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=358157#post358157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't get it when people say stuff like this. It would seem to me that the point of roleplaying is that it's a safe way to approximate the whole amazing, diverse range of contexts and experiences. Suicidally depressed people exist, and have experiences worth considering, so why <i>not</i> try to get in their mindsets?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two activities often conflated into &quot;roleplaying&quot;.<br /> <br /> One is acting. I had a great deal of fun (for about three hours, anyway) playing a homeless drug addict while almost everyone around me had godlike power.<br /> <br /> The other, however, is storytelling. And a &quot;broken&quot; player piece is a very poor fit indeed for influencing narratives in the direction the player wants to direct them,<br /> <br /> <br /> Even for actors, it can be *hard* playing somewhat suicidally depressed... if you actually make yourself think like your character, and have some of their attitudes bleed over... playing someone suicidally depressed is probably a really bad idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> And if being suicidally depressed is not something you have to *imagine*, well... it's not exactly a great fit either, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/234-superg","name":"SuperG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar234_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"451"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T03:18:36-08:00","id":358172,"title":"","content":"I think it's an interesting character to play, it's just not one that necessarily has a very long shelf life. If you're actually suicidally depressed, well, you might just kill yourself.<br /> One of my players' Lunar PC was extremely depressed... so she put herself into hibernation. Thus ending the character, in the short term at least (the other characters considered trying to solve her depression through magic, but didn't come up with anything good). Another character became extremely depressed after killing a bunch of innocent people, and killed himself. Excellent roleplaying, very interesting, but obviously not much good in the long term.<br /> But not every character has to work long-term. It's probably something to discuss with the ST.<br /> Alternatively, your character might get better.<br /> (There's also the issue of what is causing your depression: terrible things that have happened to you, or a chemical imbalance in your brain. The latter can probably be sorted out pretty quickly with Solar medicine charms. Or a Dragonblood medicine charm, for that matter.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-03-2015, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T05:18:59-08:00","id":358218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HighPriest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung#post356427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anoia, Goddess of Things That Get Stuck in Drawers</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Who is now a *major* player in my Creation on the basis of her title alone. She has dreams of taking up a much more important purview, but that job is currently occupied so she needs to arrange for an &quot;accident&quot; but can't do so on her own. I imagine her Exigent having Charms related to hiding in impossibly small spaces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T06:01:11-08:00","id":358238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuperG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=358167#post358167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if being suicidally depressed is not something you have to *imagine*, well... it's not exactly a great fit either, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't the case for everyone. I'm a writer myself, but I've never understood how other authors feel a close connection with their characters. There's always this distance- for me- between creator and creation, and I think roleplaying is something like that.<br /> Also, sometimes thinking about depression and reasoning out how it works can be healthy. What is unknown cannot be overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:45:00-08:00","id":358406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357932#post357932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I dunno. Wish fulfillment sorta thing, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did kind of mean in the specific context of a Solar being suicidally depressed because they're Anathema. Though without context it does tweak my issue of people using (poorly researched*) mental illness and neurological conditions as personality traits.<br /> <br /> *either offensive or trying so damn hard to be politically correct that the character's inclusion in the game comes across as a PSA rather than an actual person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-03-2015, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:18:37-08:00","id":358422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar. </div> </div> </div>You may be surprised to learn, then, that a lot of ancient mythological heroes went around being super depressed and stuff (though not many of them actually committed suicide).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:20:01-08:00","id":358423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar.<br /> <br /> And Again experiencing the Exaltation is something that, afterward, you should just<i> know </i>what you are, and that precludes an immaculate feeling that he's a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div> First again not every solar has known they were exalted after it happened,so that's just your table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, logically speaking &quot;I've still got all my memories, I'm still motivated by the same things, I still care about the people I care about, I don't have any memories of jacking other bodies, and I don't remember being a demon sorcerer that stole power from the sun/moon&quot; should be enough to convince one of the &quot;anathema&quot; that at least that specific part of immaculate doctrine is a load of horse shit, even if it's not enough to convince them that the whole thing is a crock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second that doesn't work. Memory alteration isn't something one is certain to know has happened to them. Yes you would know if something was forgotten that was important, but that's only if it was done sloppily. For example it would be rather awkward if you remembered swearing vengeance for the death of your best friend from childhood and had no memories of said friend outside of the 5 minutes preceding their death. But that would only key in that those details are missing it wouldn't tell you if the situation was &quot;Oh obviously someone has messed with my memories because I've only known this person for five minutes,&quot; or &quot; Well something wiped all but the last five minutes of my best friend's existence from my memory.&quot; That's a situation where its blatantly obvious memory tampering has occured. There are other ways to do it I mean there is an entire charm branch for infernals that screw with a person's memory by changing the tone the memory is remembered in. Hell it's a nigh immortal demon working for the yozi what's to say it hasn't had years writing up a complete life story for its new host just to make things easier for it. It could have spied on you for your entire life to figure out which parts of your memory need to be removed and the most effective way to remove those memories to make the most effective puppet out of you. Check a film called &quot;Dark City&quot; some time it deals a lot with how people interact with memory alteration.<br /> <br /> No memory of being a demon sorcerer who stole the power of sun and moon is simple enough. Your demon is not one of the ones who did the theft, or at least its not sharing that information with you. Considering how much the average person is told about the anathema its not exactly hard for most people to assume they didn't understand how it would work once one becomes an anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:31:33-08:00","id":358438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=357892#post357892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also character potential in just thinking the demon hasn't overwhelmed you and wanting to do what good you can before you fall to the taint. As for why you would have power before you were overtaken, well when you are still yourself mostly human actions will be taken that can be studied and used for later interactions after you've fallen. That's assuming the exalt doesn't think they'll end up with something like a coadjutor whispering in their ear. I mean it wouldn't be too hard to imagine there's a fair number of stories regarding demons and rhaksha I don't think it would be too unreasonable for a person to think its studying your actions to prevent future detection. Not to mention you not being a horrific monster might damage the immaculate faith which will be more helpful to it in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>I played a character kind of like this.<br /> <br /> He was a middle-aged Autochthonian. Had a pretty great career, had been the head Preceptor of a city and then of the nation as a whole and had basically stepped out of that role to do political outreach and had missed being in the field. His nation was attempting something like Project Razor and he was really interested in it but while he was a well-known public figure, he was &quot;past his prime&quot; and had lost a lot of political clout. Favors from old friends got him placed in charge of security of the initial expedition, though.<br /> <br /> Well, he wound up Exalting as a Solar once in Creation after saving some men at the great risk to himself and great cost to his own health. Went home to get checked up on by his nation's best doctors and while they realized it was something close to what happens when they make an Alchemical, they didn't really get it. His solum started getting a strange gold corrosion on it and they thought he had some kind of Essence-based illness native to Creation. Based on what he described from Charm use, they figured it was empowering his chakras but would eventually burn them out. So he resolved to go back into Creation and do as much as he could for God and State with the little time he had left.<br /> <br /> Of course after a certain amount of time he figured out what was happening by meeting other Solars, but the &quot;dying national figure using his last months to make our Nation the best it can be and give it the strength in the Creation that it deserves&quot; was too good a narrative for him to pass up, so he kept working in the context, vowing to one day fake his own death and slip away, leaving a heroic legacy for his children to be proud of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T11:35:47-08:00","id":358440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty insulting and dare I say ignorant statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Again experiencing the Exaltation is something that, afterward, you should just<i> know </i>what you are, and that precludes an immaculate feeling that he's a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have yet to describe what this would add to the game. I think I have gone to great detail to describe what narratives it would shut down. As far as I'm concerned you are not trying to prove your case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, logically speaking &quot;I've still got all my memories, I'm still motivated by the same things, I still care about the people I care about, I don't have any memories of jacking other bodies, and I don't remember being a demon sorcerer that stole power from the sun/moon&quot; should be enough to convince one of the &quot;anathema&quot; that at least that specific part of immaculate doctrine is a load of horse shit, even if it's not enough to convince them that the whole thing is a crock.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't remember being a demon sorcerer who jacks bodies&quot; is not evidence. As has been said, there's no statement in canon that the Immaculates say &quot;oh yeah when the Anathema gets in you, the first thing it does is explicitly announce it's there and then it gives you a ton of flashbacks of other people it's tricked, then it cackles a lot, then it completely takes control of your body and burns down an orphanage.&quot;<br /> <br /> This notion is &quot;what the christ&quot; worthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:01:14-08:00","id":358462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... do know that Depression is not just sitting at home eating ice-cream while watching netflix and feeling sad, right?<br /> <br /> Imagine a Solar that finds no satisfaction in life, that is constantly reminded in the back of his head that if he were to die, the universe and everything in it wouldn't even notice, that the world is much too big for him to ever make even the slightest difference and that his existence is basically meaningless, and no matter how hard he tries nothing he does is ever good or grande nough to find satisfaction in, <i>and yet he still <b>chooses</b> to get up in the morning and <b>try</b></i>.<br /> <br /> Nah, that's baby stuff. Easy as pie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-03-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:12:32-08:00","id":358467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div> Lioness, remind me of what the Terms of Use have to say regarding language towards other posters. Quickly please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:21:18-08:00","id":358498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're actually suicidally depressed, well, you might just kill yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wanting to die doesn't necessarily make the prospect of actually experiencing death, or at least the stuff that goes before it, any less scary, or at least physically difficult, and the variety of ways in which it can manifest can include a character who continually pursues death in reckless battles and similar circumstances that they keep winning, or at least surviving. That's before considering other social constraints, whether they be cultural taboos or stigmas attached to suicide or a personal sense that, prior to dying, one should use their great power to try and do something to help people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:29:39-08:00","id":358505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Again experiencing the Exaltation is something that, afterward, you should just<i> know </i>what you are, and that precludes an immaculate feeling that he's a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen you assert this, but haven't seen you offer up much actual support. As I see it, everyone else is arguing that it is <i>possible</i> some Exalted may experience doubt even after beholding their respective patrons, while you are the one arguing it is <i>impossible</i> or essentially so. Arguing for the more absolutist stance as you are, here, the burden of proof is on your shoulders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Took a breath, toned down the hostility a bit. 01-03-2015, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T12:43:11-08:00","id":358527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because a Solar who is Suicidally depressed is not a very heroic Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">JASON<br /> Avenge yourself, sad lover, Cr\u00e9use commands it;<br /> Do not refuse her the blood she demands;<br /> Listen to the accents of her dying voice,<br /> And fly without fear to your appointed task.<br /> To one who loves well nothing is impossible.<br /> Should you have for lair an unreachable rock,<br /> Tigress, you will die; and for all your lore,<br /> My love will see you submit to my power;<br /> My eyes will feast on the horrors of your sentence:<br /> So wishes Cr\u00e9use, so wishes my hate.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">But what! I listen to you, impotent fire!<br /> Go, do not increase the burden of my woes.<br /> To undertake a death the heavens kept for themselves,<br /> Is to prepare yet another triumph for Medea.<br /> To more effect turn your arm against yourself,<br /> And punish yourself, Jason, for not punishing her.<br /> Futile motions, in which my hopelessness entertains itself,<br /> Do not keep me from my Cr\u00e9use any longer.<br /> My queen, your beautiful soul, in leaving this place,<br /> Left me vengeance, and I leave it to the gods;<br /> Them alone, whose power equals justice,<br /> Can complete the witch's torment.<br /> Content yourself of it, dear shadow, and forgive my fire<br /> If I see you again sooner than you would wish.<br /> <br /> (He kills himself.)<br /> <br /> End of Act V.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 01-03-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T17:04:45-08:00","id":358620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=358498#post358498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wanting to die doesn't necessarily make the prospect of actually experiencing death, or at least the stuff that goes before it, any less scary, or at least physically difficult, and the variety of ways in which it can manifest can include a character who continually pursues death in reckless battles and similar circumstances that they keep winning, or at least surviving. That's before considering other social constraints, whether they be cultural taboos or stigmas attached to suicide or a personal sense that, prior to dying, one should use their great power to try and do something to help people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I was just saying you might. It's something that ought to be considered if you're going to play a character like this.<br /> There's a number of different ways to play it, but they're ones that will need to be thought through carefully.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T21:02:58-08:00","id":358804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I dislike a Solar, especially a Zenith who is attended to by Sol himself, being Suicidally but non clinically depressed because he thinks he's a monster does not sound like an appealing Solar character concept.<br /> <br /> A Solar, even one who was raised immaculate, it just doesn't make sense. &quot;Woe is me, I must be a monster for I glow gold and am ridiculously good at everything! Never mind that I have no monstrous Motivation and an urge to do virtuous deeds!&quot; The entire thing just sounds like an excuse for angst for the sake of angst, and angst for the sake of angst, is, in my t<b>otally subjective opinion,</b> is bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, this is something that only happens to NPCs off screen. That's why the gameline assumes that your PC has been Exalted for several months or so - long enough to come to terms with what he has become. You're not supposed to be <i>playing</i> a suicidally depressed Solar. Even if your character was horrified over what he had become, at the start of the game, he's gotten over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:12:59-08:00","id":358859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a Solar PC or NPC that's depressed, okay, but pick something that isn't as idiotic as &quot;I believe myself to be a monster because I glow gold and I'm really good at stuff.&quot; Because a newly Exalted Solar isn't compelled to perform monstrous actions, or evil deeds, or anything. If you were body jacked by a demon, you wouldn't think you were still you, you'd be either dead or forced to watch as something else controlled your body and spoke with your mouth. An ANathema, if the Immaculates were right about them, would probably remember being an anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off the Immaculate Order doesn't teach that Anathema immediately become monsters. Again, it teaches that they inevitably <i>become</i> monsters over time. It also doesn't teach that they are immediately mind controlled or anything, only that the soul of the Anathema will slowly replace their own over time. So the fact that a Solar doesn't turn into a monster right off the bat in no way contradicts what the Immaculate Order teaches. In fact, it's possible that the first time a Solar enters Limit Break he views that as confirmation of what the Order has taught. <br /> <br /> Second, it's entirely possible a Solar has memories of committing all sorts of horrific atrocities during the First Age (you know, the sort of things many Solars did?)<br /> <br /> So if you are told that the Anathema were terrible monsters, and you have memories of yourself performing terrible, monstrous deeds, and you're told that the soul of the dead Anathema tries to usurp control of your body, an sometimes you lose control over your actions and do stuff you normally wouldn't do, why <i>wouldn't</i> you believe what the Immaculate Order taught you? At the worst it's <i>plausible</i> that the Order is right.<br /> <br /> Again, Exaltation is doesn't immediately give you Out-Of-Character knowledge about the nature of the world. It gives you some hazy flashes, some rough memories and maybe some voices or visions. In no way does it immediately give you insight into how Creation works, or what is a lie or isn't a lie. That's up to each person to choose what do with those visions, and the idea that everyone comes to the exact same decision and nobody is influenced by their beliefs prior to Exaltation just seems kind of wonky of to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:54:59-08:00","id":358906,"title":"","content":"As to Lytek, there are good reasons why he might want to let Solars remember the terrible things their First Age Incarnations did - to make give them very vivid reasons not to do the same stuff again. <br /> <br /> But okay, how would a Solar instantly know that the Immaculate Doctrine is wrong about the Anathema, when so far none of the reasons you've given have really contradicted what the Immaculate Doctrine teaches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T01:54:34-08:00","id":358927,"title":"","content":"Where in the fluff does it say Anathema don't know they're demons anyway?<br /> All the fluff I know says they're just demons... demons with all the host's memories, and who are really, really good at lying. If they're heroic, it's for PR purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T02:39:08-08:00","id":358941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">pick something that isn't as idiotic as &quot;I believe myself to be a monster because I glow gold and I'm really good at stuff.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay! How about &quot;I believe myself to be a monster because considering the possibility that everything I've earnestly believed in and possibly made significant sacrifices to up until this point is wrong is a possibility too horrible to seriously consider. Also, considering that I wasn't born Dragon Blooded, my religiously constructed view of myself is that I'm not actually worthy of or suitable to possessing great power yet, and so believe that it will ineivtably go wrong due to the fallability of humanity, exacerbated by the fact that I would also believe that my condition is due to the fact that I was a sinful Immaculate, making me doubly dangerous&quot;. Meanwhile, the Unconquered Sun is off sitting on his cloud, thinking &quot;okay, let's see what interesting things this person does are&quot;. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the kind of idiot incapable of thinking for themselves in which case they probably lack the drive to go out and earn a Solar Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Demetheus was never really too bright or assertive, yet he still had a moment of clarity that ended with him being Exalted. Your odious designations aside, people can still be complicated enough that they do things that go against what they think is their better judgement, or just on the impulse of the moment. Tom Sawyer continuing to think it's unforgivably sinful to assist a black man even while he resolves to do it does not make him an idiot, nor is it a contradiction. Hell, a moment of heroism like that seems like it would be especially fitting for the Solar milieu. The idea that Solars are universally driven and doubtless cuts off so many interesting possibilities for what are supposed to be the most versatile group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T03:06:10-08:00","id":358987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suicidally depressed Solars are a thing that shouldn't happen <i><b>at all</b></i> though, at least not because they were Immaculate-If a solat thinks &quot;better kill myself because I'm an anathema, even though an anathema certainly wouldn't think thoughts like that and I don't feel any compulsion to act the way the immaculate order says I should&quot; then he's either to thoroughly brainwashed by immaculate doctrine to do the sort of thing that would earn him a Solar Exaltation, was already suicidal when they Exalted(not touching it), or they're the kind of idiot incapable of thinking for themselves in which case they probably lack the drive to go out and earn a Solar Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: you don't &quot;earn&quot; a Celestial Exaltation. It's not something you get by virtue of putting in time and effort. Many thousands of &quot;worthy&quot; people exist for every Celestial Exaltation. Instead, you're given the greatest gift that can ever be given, with no strings attached, because one of the greatest gods in the world felt a connection to you, felt something within you resonate with its infinite glory. And in that moment of connection, it deigned to pass a reflection of its power to you.<br /> <br /> You can be a devout Immaculate and have a moment that fundamentally connects with the nature of the Unconquered Sun. I see that one mortal monk who stands up to Deled being in a particularly good moment to receive some kind of blessing for standing up for the weak when it would be easier to keep his mouth shut.<br /> <br /> Let's not talk about it as if someone can work real hard at Exalting Celestial and make it happen due to that hard work.<br /> <br /> Let's also remember that Intelligence 1 characters are perfectly supported by the rules. And you're hyperbolizing Immaculate doctrine - as has been said, the Immaculates don't tell mortals not to go forth and be awesome, or be ambitious, or work hard, or corner a niche in a field they excel in. They mainly reference a spiritual hierarchy with the DBs on top, and not trying to reach beyond your station by dealing with gods or wielding magical items or thinking that you'd do a better job running the world than the demigods do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a Solar PC or NPC that's depressed, okay, but pick something that isn't as idiotic as &quot;I believe myself to be a monster because I glow gold and I'm really good at stuff.&quot; Because a newly Exalted Solar isn't compelled to perform monstrous actions, or evil deeds, or anything. If you were body jacked by a demon, you wouldn't think you were still you, you'd be either dead or forced to watch as something else controlled your body and spoke with your mouth. An Anathema, if the Immaculates were right about them, would probably remember being an anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing. If you were kind of a middling thief who picked pockets in a marketplace and lives hand-to-mouth and suddenly have the power to sneak in and out of the imperial mint and steal money beyond your wildest dreams, wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If you were a gladiator who did pretty well and now can drop people in 1 punch instead of 10, thus making it less likely that you'd get injured, wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If you're a local trader getting pushed out by the Guild and you can now wheel and deal with the bureaucrats on a level the Guild can't even imagine to give yourself favorable state contracts, wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If you were a lawyer who did ok but not great and suddenly had the power to be more convincing than your greatest rivals and win every case you tried and pick up high-rolling clients in the process, wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> If you and your family were constantly under threat of dangerous force from some group, and now had the power to permanently end that threat without the possibility of getting caught, wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> These are things that the Immaculates might call &quot;alien desires imposed on you by a demon.&quot; They are in fact your own <i>very human</i> desires, your subconscious recognizing what is now possible through the grace bestowed on you and pushing you to take what has been denied you, to punish those who have transgressed you, to sit at the table instead of begging in the street. It's <i>very</i> easy for the Immaculates to cast these as the outside influence of a demon, and it's easy for other mortals to cast judgment on you, because people certainly would view achieving these desires as selfish and unfair and morally reprehensible (even if they would certainly do these things themselves given the power to do so).<br /> <br /> Evil is relative. You smash a baker's shop window at night to steal bread to feed your starving family. You may not think that's an evil deed but the baker surely does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't remember being a demon sorcerer who stole power from the gods and jacked somebodies body, then you probably aren't</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a huge logical fallacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I imagine if someone was possesed by a spirit trying to take their body, they'd feel some sort of evil presence about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again your headcanon about how possession should feel is not relevant because it's not supported by anything in any canon text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Idea that someone could still believe the anathema BS after Exalting themselves and <i>realizing</i> it requires far to many leaps of logic for one individual to make for me to take it seriously in anything but a parody situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So your neighborhood in a Realm satrapy is being terrorized/shaken down by branch of the local guard that has a Realm patron - these guardsmen ride with him on his hunts, or whatever, and his patronage gives them general impunity to local law. The Realm doesn't care that this is happening at all, because it's not affecting the tax flow. This has happened for years and you have made the payments from your meager income, and still your family and friends get hassled for more. You now have the power to kill all of those gang members at night, without any real chance of being identified or caught. You do it; your neighborhood is a safer place, but you've committed multiple murders to do so.<br /> <br /> Can you not see where a person might believe this power has changed them? That they're no longer the person they thought they were? That their family is safer, but at what cost to their soul? Or their perceived morality?<br /> <br /> These are tough questions that deserve to be explored in the context of gaining superhuman levels of skillful mastery. There's nothing gained by sweeping them under the rug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you want a Solar who thinks he's a monster-have him kill a loved one in the midst of a Limit Break. You want inner turmoil as a result of an immaculate faithful Exalting? &quot;If my faith was mistaken about this, then what else might they be mistaken about?&quot; Both of those are options that make infinitely more sense than a Solar thinking he's a monster because a a sham religion that he's living proof is wrong on at least one thing, which is the only thing that's relevant to the question of whether or not he's a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it off-putting that you're telling people what kind of identity-crisis narratives you'll deign to find &quot;appropriate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T03:12:25-08:00","id":358989,"title":"","content":"You may not be intentionally earning it, but it's not a gift given at random either.<br /> <br /> Billy Batson had no intention of becoming a superhero when he was chosen to be Captain Marvel, sure, but he certainly didn't get selected by sitting on his ass either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T03:22:11-08:00","id":358991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=358989#post358989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not be intentionally earning it, but it's not a gift given at random either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think my post implied it was random? That whole bit about &quot;connection with the god,&quot; etc? That's extrapolated directly from Perfect Soul's Exaltation scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T04:59:44-08:00","id":359013,"title":"","content":"Blech, sorry, I'm tired and didn't read that far - to be fair, there were enough &quot;Cosmic Lottery&quot; posts on this board not long ago\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T05:18:22-08:00","id":359019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=359013#post359013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blech, sorry, I'm tired and didn't read that far - to be fair, there were enough &quot;Cosmic Lottery&quot; posts on this board not long ago\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, no worries, we've all been there. And true nuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T09:41:34-08:00","id":359238,"title":"","content":"As for 'not knowing you are possessed'...<br /> <br /> There is a folk story about meeting a demon in the crossroads. A version I heard was, there was a criminal who was so strong and confident, that he bragged he was not afraid of anything. And so, when he heard that you meet the devil in a certain crossroad at midnight, he told everyone he would wait there, for the devil to show up. Which he did, and the devil never did show up. So, he came out, bragging everyone else is a coward, and only he had the guts to do it... and, since the devil is a lie, there's nothing to be afraid of, no punishment waiting for you. He became more and more cruel, utterly vile... showing that he did meet the devil in the crossroads. And the way of the devil was to not appear.<br /> <br /> Same thing here? To know all the tenets of religion are a lie, to be given carte blanche to act in the world... that can be seen as in and of itself damning. <br /> <br /> I imagine many an Immaculate-Born Solar rode the rush of power, defeating the local Satrap or Dragon-Blooded, and only sunk in to them they might truly be anathema when they parade the corpse to people, expecting adoration, and see only fear in their eyes instead. Or the twilight that gets told to look around to see that he is anathema, when he is surrounded by demons and sat on a throne of singing flesh.<br /> <br /> Such moments are far too resonant to want to remove them from the game entirely.<br /> <br /> Hell, it is against the very nature of the game; it doesn't tell the player what is right and what is wrong, who are the good guys and the bad guys, why would the character have more certainty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T11:12:12-08:00","id":359328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Straw Nihilism fallacy. Someone who discovers or decides that there is no reward or punishment after death and that life has no inherent meaning is just as likely to decide to give his own life meaning through great deeds of good as he is through great deeds of evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>... yes? I said that CAN be seen as damning. I said it is POSSIBLE. Not that it is the only way.<br /> <br /> You, however, have asked how it is even possible to think you are possessed while still having your own thoughts.<br /> <br /> I answered.<br /> <br /> And you are clearly not arguing in good faith if your answer is that someone can think of it some other way. Well, duh. That's where PCs come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T11:22:17-08:00","id":359330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the Anathema do not start as evil but become evil, the fact that they are, according to immaculate doctrine, body stealing sorcerers, means that an Anathema not acting evil is merely pretending to be who they once were. It makes absolutely no logical sense for the Anathema in question to think that <i>they're</i> the person they body jacked, and if the anathema in question does not actually steal the persons body but merely grants them power and influences them-then they can both be resisted and therefore are not, in fact, inevitably going to turn evil <i>or </i>body jacking demons, and it means that regardless of why the Doctrine is wrong on the subject of Anathema, they were wrong on the subject of anathema.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Slowly replaces your soul&quot; is not the same as &quot;body-snatcher&quot;.<br /> Since, in Exalted, people have 2 souls (y'know, Hun and Po), and on top of that there's a <i>huge</i> difference between &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;mind&quot;. Having one or both of your souls replaced by a thing that makes you want to exert your power and slowly twists the rest of you doesn't mean your brain or thoughts are altered.<br /> <br /> Also, you're grossly underestimating the degree to which people want to cling to their beliefs, no matter how mistaken they are. People don't generally want to accept that the thing they've believed their etire life is a lie, and will search for (and find, through confirmation bias) ways to rationalize away any discrepencies.<br /> <br /> Adding to that, Solars have augmented powers of self-delusion (Integrity can just as easily serve to strengthen existing and erroneous beliefs and prejudices, There are examples of Charisma + Presence rolls being used to convince yourself of things (e.g. to build intimacies of &quot;I have been turned into a demon&quot;), a botched Perception + Investigation (introspection) roll for which you have no excellency could easily make you think you feel things that aren't there).<br /> <br /> Lastly, &quot;transcendent religious experiences&quot; are something the fairfolk can inflict upon you simply by feeding on you, as well as through other charms. Just because it &quot;feels right&quot; doesn't mean it's not what the demon wants you to think.<br /> <br /> So no, not <i>every single solar ever</i> is going to figure out their life has been a lie at the exact moment of their exaltation, even though some might.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Straw Nhilism fallacy. Someone who discovers or decides that there is no reward or punnishment after death and that life has no inherant meaning is just as likely to decide to give his own life meaning through great deeds of good as he is through great deeds of evil. </div> </div> </div>It can be seen as confirmation that you are indeed posessed, as the demon inside you is trying to convince you that your life has been a lie, by giving you visions of false truths and fake transcendence that will only lead you onto the path of sin.<br /> <br /> The amount of things people can make up to hurt themselves out of self-loathing can be staggering. Exalted, especially Solars, really aren't exempt from that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Another example of the powers of delusion: Back in the colonial days of Quebec, anyone who hadn't attended Confession in seven years was thought to be a werewolf, and people <i>believed themselves to actually be werewolves</i> despite there being no such Void-damned thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":43,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","user":"Fata-Ku","date":". 01-04-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:04:37-08:00","id":359783,"title":"","content":"It's not that out there for a newly Exalted Solar to kill themselves, thinking they're a demon. It varies by person, obviously, and I suspect it's somewhat less likely for Zeniths and less likely overall than the spread of the Faith would suggest, but it's totally a thing that happens. This is one reason you don't generally play newly Exalted Solars! Grabowski's comments on that are <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/WhatDoTheyDo\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T23:41:19-08:00","id":359926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why, but I've gotten a sudden urge to convert Exalted Modern to the new edition, just so I can make an Exigent of Boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm well you would have a case for making a lot of elsewhere based charms. Actually you could probably do it in base setting exalted. You just wouldn't have as powerful a patron in the time of tumult as you would in the modern world. This is assuming that we count storage and shipping crates as boxes of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T04:24:24-08:00","id":360106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Those are all<i> extremely</i> human reactions, and the Immaculates are full of horse shit if they say &quot;The same stuff you've been doing, but better&quot; are alien desires imposed by a demon. Anybody who experiences it first hand and thinks about it rationally for more than a few seconds is going to know that that's wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look around you. Right now. Go read some news articles. Go visit a couple of random churches, maybe visit a couple of protests. Go visit the Phelps folks. Go look at the comment section of any random video on youtube. <br /> Are you really under the impression that people come to their beliefs by rational decisions? Even now, when science and reason are such a huge factor in our lives? You seem to be someone who thinks rationality, science and reason are important. Go read what actual scientists, researchers and very educated thinkers are discovering about how we actually think about things. Go read some Steven Pinker books. You are drastically not understanding how people come about their beliefs and drastically overstating how easy it is for anyone to think rationally about their beliefs. Yes, even you.<br /> <br /> That's now by the way. In the bronze age? With actual acts of wonder and magic that defy reason on a regular basis? Yeah, I'm think that rationally figuring out your beliefs is not quite the obvious or easy thing you are suggesting.<br /> <br /> For example - look at the Mohammed experience in this thread. The founder of one of the single largest religions in our world had a religious experience with the divine that called him to action such that he created an incredibly huge and history impacting religion. His first reactions weren't certitude or rational thought. It was awe, fear, and doubt. Even wondering if he had been possessed.<br /> <br /> Mohammed is frequently cited as an inspiration for Zenith caste Exalts. Yet you are suggesting that that very inspiration is invalid - because apparently the first reaction to being visited by the King of the Gods and doubting everything that you have learned your whole life should be to rationally consider your beliefs? That's just completely not understanding how people work.<br /> <br /> I think part of it comes from the trend that 3e is trying to stop. The trend of removing the mystical from the game and making it one big scientific, rational place where everything is explained, the gods come down and just casually chat with you and everything is explained away. You are essentially demonstrating why that perspective drastically weakened the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4671-thehappyanarchist","name":"TheHappyAnarchist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T04:32:22-08:00","id":360107,"title":"","content":"I've been following this forum and thread for a bit and I thought I'd register and make a post here to say that I play a suicidally depressed Zenith. The only reason he hasn't killed himself yet is his own fear of death. I've been having a great time portraying this character, the group's having fun. It really rustled my jimmies when the character concept that I am having lots of fun with was deemed 'idiotic' and 'stupid' and 'bullshit' and unappealing.<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, people like different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4672-hog-of-war","name":"Hog of War","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:35:56-08:00","id":360166,"title":"","content":"Oh, join the club. The Venn diagram of &quot;things that ruined 2e according to this forum&quot; and &quot;things that got me playing Exalted in the first place&quot; is practically a goddamn circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:41:37-08:00","id":360175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why, but I've gotten a sudden urge to convert Exalted Modern to the new edition, just so I can make an Exigent of Boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;I AM THE BOX GHOS... EXALT! YES, I AM TOTALLY THE LATTER THING!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:19:53-08:00","id":360195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hog of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/356427-unwanted-exigent-exaltations-or-no-thanks-god-of-buffalo-dung?p=360107#post360107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been following this forum and thread for a bit and I thought I'd register and make a post here to say that I play a suicidally depressed Zenith. The only reason he hasn't killed himself yet is his own fear of death. I've been having a great time portraying this character, the group's having fun. It really rustled my jimmies when the character concept that I am having lots of fun with was deemed 'idiotic' and 'stupid' and 'bullshit' and unappealing.<br /> <br /> Maybe, just maybe, people like different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Internet commentary tends to frown upon character concepts and motivations rooted in emotions rather than cold, hard rationality. It's a large part of why 2e went the way it did.<br /> <br /> I am actually playing a suicidal Zenith at the moment, myself, though not for religious reasons; Almas Ogun has a rare disease from Gem which causes his body to slowly turn to gemstones (he has Diamond eyes, making his vision multfaceted and useless, for instance; he has to use Sensory Acuity Prana just to see normally) and believes it is incurable (since he had one too many charlatans try to do so before he Exalted), so all he wants is to die well before the disease takes him, much to the consternation of his Twilight lover and Wood Aspect doctor. Thanks to this being 1e and his Nature being Martyr, I actually get mechanically rewarded for ridiculous feats of self-sacrifice in the path to a Good Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T09:46:06-08:00","id":360252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why, but I've gotten a sudden urge to convert Exalted Modern to the new edition, just so I can make an Exigent of Boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will they be capable of hiding in the box while making everyone think the box is supposed to be there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T09:51:21-08:00","id":360254,"title":"","content":"Durable Serpent Concealment Stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:44:42-08:00","id":360461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">-that. Or, um, actually it would be more &quot;I am the Box God! Divine Master of all things that contain other things! I have chosen you to be my Champion!<br /> Will it get you to stop yelling?&quot;<br /> &quot;Maybe!&quot;<br /> &quot;Then I accept.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need someone who can do a good BRIAN BLESSED impersonation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:40:54-08:00","id":360535,"title":"","content":"Surely that GPS program that uses his voice could be repurposed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:52:18-08:00","id":361017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Chances are, none of them have experienced, first hand, a divine miracle on par with The Exaltation. By all means, that's the sort of thing that, once you've realized what is going on, you can't just confuse for anything other than a powerful divine miracle.<br /> 2. Chances are, those people are among the groups who A.are the 80% of Americans who claim to be christian or jewish and are among the 80% who claim to have never read a religious text, and therefore do not understand the religion they claim to be a member of. I'm sure there are people like that in other nations as well, but I do not know the numbers.<br /> 3. Chances are, if 2 isn't true, they belong to a group that cherry picks lines from the religious text in question, without knowing what the line really means, and takes them out of context to support a hateful agenda.<br /> 4. Youtube is filled to the brim with people who fake beliefs they don't have just so they can get into fights and piss people off. That's not evidence for anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>DUDE! They just cited freaking Mohammed! A guy who had a religious experience so powerful that he created a new major religion that is practiced worldwide! That is a direct divine miracle and his first reactions were doubt, fear, and awe. He also isn't alone among religious figures. Jesus was described as filled with doubt several times. So where several biblical prophets. I don't know enough about specific other religions, but I'd wager that many of them doubt their divine experiences as well, or at least express confusion. So no, experiencing a divine miracle - arguably even more of one than the miracle of Exaltation - does not mean you automatically have no doubts, have no confusion about what is going on. <br /> <br /> As for number 2 - yes that is exactly my point. The overwhelming majority of people don't pick their beliefs by rationally weighing them. Heck, even most of the people who think they pick their beliefs rationally do not. If you agree with that, then why are you suggesting that the majority of people Exalting will react to that by rationally weighing the evidence? Even as an atheist who values reason highly, after an experience like that my first thoughts would not be rational. Heck, as someone who has read up on how our brains actually think and weigh evidence, I'm under no delusions that I would ever be able to rationally consider it. It's almost a matter of luck at that point.<br /> <br /> As for youtube being filled with fake comments, sure. Go to any family dinner then. Go walk on the street and talk to random people on the bus. Look at the weight of people believing in alien abductions or that the pyramids were made by aliens and can give you psychic powers. <br /> <br /> Better yet, again - go read the research that has been done on how we think and how we come to decisions. Anyone thinking that the majority of the human race is inherently rational, or that people having divine experiences are going to think about those experiences rationally is simply completely unaware of how human minds work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4671-thehappyanarchist","name":"TheHappyAnarchist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T17:45:59-08:00","id":363945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this off topic conversation has gone on long enough. You're not going to convince me that Suicidally depressed Former Immaculate Solars should be a thing, and I'm not going to convince any of you that they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Can we go back to talking about undignified exigencies? Please?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be the Chosen of Lacks-For-Talk (god of That Awkward Moment When Strangers First Meet). I <i>am</i> that moment, in-universe and out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}